Error [jet.ViewOutlivesOwner]: This view points into `mapped`, which this function owns
  --> tests/ui/mapped_window_outlives_its_map.jet:6:12
    |
  6 |     mapped.window_len(0, 1)
    |            ^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: `mapped` is made here and freed when the function returns, so a read window into it would outlive what owns it — there'd be nothing left to look at
 Fix: Return an owned copy with `place.copy()` (for example `value[a..b].copy()`), or accept the source as a parameter so the caller keeps owning it
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E2305

Error [jet.ViewOutlivesOwner]: Returned views need a stable owner relationship
  --> tests/ui/mapped_window_outlives_its_map.jet:10:13
    |
 10 |     window: leak("table.txt") ?? return
    |             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: Each public `View`/`ViewMut` slot must name a bounded set of receiver, parameter, or static sources that stay live; this return did not prove those sources
 Fix: Return a view derived from parameters or the receiver on every path, keep the view local, or return an owned copy with `.copy()`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E2305
